derived from the projects listed below, each distributed under the MIT License.
The original copyright notices are reproduced here as required by that license.

dsh-workbuddy-websearch
  https://github.com/arnen7000/DSH-Workbuddy-WebSearch
  Copyright (c) 2026 XingLang & WorkBuddy (小研)
  Licensed under the MIT License.
  Used as a runtime peer dependency (its platform, credential, and region
  capabilities are called, not vendored), and as the reference for the region
  selection and credential-state logic reimplemented in buildFallbackBridge().

dsh-workbuddy-connect
  https://github.com/corrinehu/dsh-workbuddy-connect
  Copyright (c) 2026 Corrine Hu
  Licensed under the MIT License.
  Not depended on directly; its CredentialStore is reached only indirectly,
  through dsh-workbuddy-websearch's optional enhancement path.

@deepseek-ai/dsh-web and @deepseek-ai/dsh-web-fetch-http
  Copyright (c) DeepSeek
  Licensed under the MIT License.
  Contract-level dependencies reached through the harness itself; no source
  is copied. The local-fetch fallback instantiates web-fetch-http's exported
  HttpFetchProvider.

WorkBuddy desktop application (app.asar)
  Copyright (c) Tencent / WorkBuddy
  No code is copied, bundled, or modified. The /agenttool/v1/webfetch request
  shape was determined by inspecting the locally installed application, and
  this plugin only uses that documented-by-inspection endpoint together with
  the user's own sign-in state. All rights to the application, its protocols,
  and its endpoints remain with their owners.

See CREDITS.md for the per-source breakdown of what was referenced and what is
